    "turn_text": "Hello, this is Ambassador Jim Rose of Pepp, your host today for American Ambassadors Live, the podcast on international affairs sponsored by the Council of American Ambassadors in Washington, D.C. The Council is the Association of Non-Career U.S. Ambassadors, who have represented America under Presidents from John F. Kennedy from Donald Trump. Our guest today is U.S. Congressman Francis Rooney of Florida. He serves on the House Foreign Affairs Committee and its Western Hemisphere Subcommittee. He's with us today. He's also U.S. Ambassador to the Holy See under President George W. Bush. And he's the author of a fascinating book about the Catholic Church's role in international affairs. It's called The Global Vatican. Welcome, Ambassador, Congressman. Ambassador, thank you for having me. Oh, it's great. It really is a fascinating book. And it has so much in it that we can't cover all of it in this brief time. I want to start off with some of the history of the relations between the United States and the Holy See. There are two themes that came across strongly as I was reading that history. One was the anti-Catholicism of the United States, which most of us who are Americans, particularly American Catholics, know about. but also the anti-democratic attitudes of the Vatican. Could you talk a little bit about that clash of cultures?",
