    "turn_idx": 55,
    "turn_text": "And so when I was ambassador to Romania, at least when I first got there, the Nuncio was the senior member of the diplomatic corps, so he was the dean of the diplomatic corps. And I had some interactions with him. I'm sure not as many as you had with folks at the Vatican being ambassador to the Holy See. But one of the things that impressed me And I want you to talk a little bit about the culture of diplomacy with the Vatican, is because the Nitzios have this dual role, and the Catholic Church is both an international, it's a nation, it's a country, but it also is made up of members who are citizens of the host country. My experience was that the Nutsio tend to know a lot more about a lot of things than a lot of the rest of us ambassadors did, because he had a lot more sources of information shall we say.",
