    "turn_idx": 110,
    "turn_text": "Well, this is the core of Holy See's diplomacy. It's focused on these fundamental principles that are key to the Church. Natural rights of man, human dignity. There's one really smart guy, Cardinal Tehran, who used to be high in the State Department over there, used to say that the Holy See diplomacy serves as a moral authority to contest systems which corrode the dignity of the person and threaten world peace. So it's all focused on humanity. It's a very humanistic form of diplomacy. And of course, as you know, it's soft power. They don't have any armies. But one of the great ironies there, Stalin said, where's the Pope's army? It was actually a pope that brought Stalin's successors down.",
